**What the feedback showed about the research.** The researcher persona's main point wasn't about the site. The project is now held back by the 12 decisions waiting on you and by the fact that no outside human has seen any of its results, not by a lack of data. Outreach has gone to you as a bare yes/no four times since 11-08 with nothing ready to send, and nothing happened. So this time I wrote the note itself: `Synchronism/Research/proposals/draft_note_to_refracted_gravity_authors_llr_bounds_the_smoothing_length_20261127.md`. It tells the RG authors that lunar laser ranging (LLR) rules out all three of their published fits. That holds at smoothing lengths of 1–10 pc, which their galaxy fits need. It then asks them what that smoothing length is meant to be. I left out the BBN result on purpose: it was computed for the framework's own law, not for RG's, so including it would claim more than we checked. The explorer has a topic to re-run the numbers before anything goes out.

